        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="classjuce_1_1String" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/tagfile.xml">juce::String</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>groupId</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Serialises <computeroutput>artwork</computeroutput> as Svg markup, shifted by (deltaX, deltaY). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Zero in both <computeroutput>deltaX</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>deltaY</computeroutput> writes <computeroutput>artwork</computeroutput> unchanged via <ref refid="structjam_1_1XmlDocument_1a67e65a29647faa906d56a87d691e8bcb" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">jam::Xml::getText()</ref>. Otherwise, the element&apos;s tag selects an entry of the shifted-attribute table: path translates its <computeroutput>d</computeroutput> data, rect shifts <computeroutput>x</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>y</computeroutput>, ellipse and circle shift <computeroutput>cx</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>cy</computeroutput>, and line shifts both end points. The element is written with those attributes overridden. A tag absent from the table fails the console application, naming <computeroutput>groupId</computeroutput> and the tag in the message.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>artwork</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The artwork element to serialise. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>deltaX</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Horizontal shift in glyph-sheet units. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>deltaY</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Vertical shift in glyph-sheet units. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>groupId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The glyph group&apos;s id, named in the failure message when <computeroutput>artwork&apos;s</computeroutput> tag is absent from the table. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The artwork element&apos;s Svg markup, coordinates shifted by the delta. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
